# crabagent / Sandcrab landing page

A static landing page selling Sandcrab (open-source sandboxing for production AI agents),
fronted by crabagent. Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS, built with Vite. The build output is plain
files with relative paths, so it can be served from any folder on any static server.

```sh
npm install
npm run dev       # dev server on :5173
npm run build     # writes the static site to dist/
npm run preview   # serves dist/ on :5173
```

Serve `dist/` with anything (`npx serve dist`, nginx, S3, GitHub Pages, a sub-folder, ...).
It uses ES modules, so open it over http(s), not `file://`.

## Layout

| Path | What |
| --- | --- |
| `index.html` | All the content. `<!--glyph:name-->` inlines `src/glyphs/name.svg` at build time. |
| `src/style.css` | Palette tokens (from the kit's `symbology.html`), light + dark, responsive layout, self-hosted `@font-face`. |
| `src/main.js` | Theme toggle (auto / light / dark), copy buttons, scroll reveal, lazy 3D mounting. |
| `src/kit3d/` | Copy of the Sandcrab three.js kit (`src/` + vendored three.js r186). Scenes used: `molt` (hero), `wire`, `burrow`. Only change vs the original: a `@vite-ignore` on the default fallback URL. |
| `src/fonts/` | Space Grotesk, Inter, JetBrains Mono (latin + latin-ext, SIL OFL licences alongside). |
| `src/glyphs/` | The kit's line glyphs (recoloured by CSS for dark mode). |
| `public/assets/crab/` | The kit's `.webp` illustrations: posters, no-WebGL fallbacks and figures. |

No CDNs: fonts, three.js and images are all in the build.

## Behaviour notes

- 3D scenes mount lazily (the hero immediately, the others near the viewport). Without WebGL the
  illustration stays. With `prefers-reduced-motion` the kit renders a still frame.
- Theme follows the system by default; the nav button cycles auto -> light -> dark and remembers the choice.
- Copy in the page was written from the kit's walkthrough: Docker dev backend is dev/CI only (shared kernel,
  explicit opt-in); Firecracker is "next".
